.TITLE "security"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages keychains, certificates, encryption, and other security-related operations
on macOS. This command-line utility provides access to the macOS Keychain,
allowing users to store and retrieve passwords, cryptographic keys, and digital
certificates. It is a fundamental tool for system security.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**keychain**

.DIV "TLDR"
**security find-generic-password -s "__Service Name__" -a "__Account__" -w**
Finds and prints the password for a generic password item with a given __Service Name__ and __Account__.
> __"Service Name"__: The service name of the password item. | __"Account"__: The account name associated with the password.

**security add-generic-password -s "__Service Name__" -a "__Account__" -w "__Password__"**
Adds a generic password item to the default keychain.
> __"Service Name"__: The service name for the new password item. | __"Account"__: The account name for the new password item. | __"Password"__: The password to store.

**security delete-generic-password -s "__Service Name__" -a "__Account__"**
Deletes a generic password item from the default keychain.
> __"Service Name"__: The service name of the password item to delete. | __"Account"__: The account name associated with the password.

**security list-keychains**
Lists the keychains in the current user's search list.
> 

**security unlock-keychain __~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db__**
Unlocks a specific keychain, allowing programmatic access to its items.
> __~/Library/Keychains/login.keychain-db__: The path to the keychain file.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The `security` command is critical for managing sensitive information on macOS.
Always handle passwords and keys with care. For complex operations, consider
referencing the full `man security` page due to the depth of its functionality.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:defaults**

documentation: https://ss64.com/osx/security.html
